  "question": {
    "text": "A beam of light of wavelength $\\lambda$ falls on a metal having work function $\\phi$ placed in a magnetic field $B$. The most energetic electrons, perpendicular to the field are bent in circular arcs of radius R. If the experiment is performed for different values of $\\lambda$, then $B^2$ vs. $\\frac{1}{\\lambda}$ graph will look like (keeping all other quantities constant)"
